  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark grabs your ID at 3 am, goes to Waffle House, and insults people.\n \n+* html2text.py doesn't handle the `<sup>` tag. wsbuglink:20020[].\n+* Fuzz job assertion: randpkt-2024-10-05-7200.pcap. wsbuglink:20110[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -57,18 +60,28 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.7.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.8.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+DMP\n+GTP\n+HTTP\n+LwM2M-TLV\n+SSyncP\n+TCP\n+Thrift\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+BLF\n+ERF\n+pcap\n+--\n \n === Updated File Format Decoding Support\n \n",
